// ---- app config: the V2 switches and the AI switch (foundation ADR-0014, ADR-0015) ----
// One document, `appConfig/flags`: a boolean per V2 capability. Anybody may
// read it — it is a list of switches, not anybody's data — and nobody writes
// it from a client; Daniel sets it in the console. `appConfig/ai` is the AI
// kill switch and the monthly caps, read only by Functions; a client has no
// reason to know the caps, and must never be able to raise them. Any other id
// here is closed, so the collection cannot quietly grow into a place for data.
// `aiEmulator/{feature}` holds the canned model answers the Functions emulator
// uses; it has no rule, so no client reads or writes it.
match /appConfig/{configId} {
  allow get: if configId == 'flags';
  allow list: if false;
  allow write: if false;
}
